    {
      "id": 31884,
      "name": "Craig",
      "username": "Craig",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/{size}/2150_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-05-26T13:24:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This raises an interesting question, though. I can’t remember what environment card it is off the top of my head that says a player may skip their turn to destroy it, but is that decision made at the start of that player’s turn or in some nebulous space before their turn actually begins?</p>",
