      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/{size}/2150_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-05-26T16:17:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;TheJayMann&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"TheJayMann\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m nearly certain the card says something along the lines of “At the start of a player’s turn, that player may skip the rest if ‘his’ turn to destroy this card.”  Thus, it would occur during the normal start of turn phase, processed in card order (so any start of turn effects that was played after this card woulc be skipped if you chose to skip your turn at that time).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ah, that answers that. I obviously didn’t have it in front of me, so I couldn’t recall the exact wording.</p>\n<p>At any rate, the guys in the lab have done a pretty good job of making sure we know exactly what things happen when and in what order, if you read cards exactly as written. There aren’t really any exceptions to the basics, which I love.</p>",
